#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.11"
# dependencies = ["textual>=8", "packaging"]
# ///
# This file was edited with the assistance of an AI model and requires human review from the contributor.
"""dlmeta — overview and updating of all datalab deployment repos.

  dlmeta              interactive TUI (same as `dlmeta tui`)
  dlmeta tui [--to REF]
  dlmeta status       table of every deployment (local state + ledger + last probe)
  dlmeta run          run a command in several deployments, e.g. `dlmeta run -- make maintenance`
  dlmeta discover     read each repo's api_url from its encrypted inventory (needs rbw)
  dlmeta probe        query each deployment's public /info endpoint for its live version
  dlmeta dashboard    write dashboard.html (runs `probe` first unless --no-probe)

Configuration is read from $DLMETA_CONFIG (default ~/.config/dlmeta/config.toml, see
dlmeta.example.toml). Deployments are the repos with an ansible/playbook.yml listed under
`deployments`, each entry being either a repo or a folder of repos (default
~/repos/datalab/deployments, overridden by $DLMETA_DEPLOYMENTS_DIR). Deployments listed under
[inactive] are hidden unless asked for.

State is kept in $DLMETA_STATE_DIR (or `state_dir` in the config, default ~/.local/state/dlmeta):
deploy records come from the deployment_ledger callback (runs/<repo>.jsonl), probe results are
appended to runs/_probes.jsonl, discovered URLs are cached in deployments.json and the output of
`dlmeta run` is written to logs/.
"""

